    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the biggest cost owners miss when comparing management fees?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The missing cost is often not the management fee alone. It is everything around it: marketplace fees, payment costs, discounting, and day-to-day execution. Seascape's current benchmark shows an observed 13.4% Airbnb host-fee cost compared with an approximate 2.9% direct payment cost."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can direct bookings improve what an owner keeps?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, when they replace higher-cost marketplace bookings. Seascape's current Gulf Coast operating set has already routed $119,923 through direct bookings, but the report treats that upside as an example rather than a universal guarantee."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should owners choose the lowest management fee?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not automatically. A lower headline fee can still leave you behind if pricing is soft, booking channels are expensive, or local operations erode review quality and rate power. The better comparison is what you actually keep after management fee, booking costs, and execution risk."
      }
    }
  ]
}</script>

